Package: pbs-sync-auth-client
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Florian Taeger <florian@taeger.cc>
Depends: systemd
Recommends: proxmox-backup-server
Homepage: https://github.com/ftaeger/pbs-sync-auth
Description: Guarded offsite push auth client for Proxmox Backup Server
 Performs a mutual HMAC-SHA256 challenge-response against the pbs-sync-auth
 server and, only on success, triggers a PBS push sync job on the local
 (source) Proxmox Backup Server. Runs as a systemd daemon with a configurable
 check interval and minimum backup interval.
 .
 The shared secret is deliberately not shipped: create
 /etc/pbs-sync-auth/secret.key with the same content as on the server, adjust
 /etc/pbs-sync-auth/client.conf, then enable the pbs-sync-auth.service.
